Greetings,

I hope you're doing well.

Last Friday Thorwin agents came to my suite to identify a solution for the
upcoming removal of laundry services and storage facilities with the goal
of installing en suite laundry machines.

It has been 129 days since my previous email to you regarding this issue
and I have not received any clarity on what your plan is.

The electrical system in my suite is from the 1950s, there is no storage
space for a washer/dryer in the suite, and if there were some space with
which to place the units it would require opening up the floor boards and
extending the pipes.

My understanding is that Thorwin has full intention of removing the storage
and laundry services, which I have paid for in my entire residency here,
forcing a renovation on me that will negatively affect my quality of living
through the day to day work, reducing my storage space capabilities, and of
course, increasing the rent far above what it should be if provincial
guidelines were followed in good faith.

I want to be clear that I do not want en suite laundry services and I do
not want my storage space removed.

I look forward to hearing your solutions.

Thank you,
Evan Rosner
10-585 Corydon Ave




